  {
    "id": "2026-09-15-johnson-107",
    "date": "2026-09-15",
    "addressed_to": "Speaker of the House Mike Johnson",
    "led_by": [],
    "summary": "The letter urges Speaker Johnson to keep the House in session (the press-release version says \"immediately reconvene\") until Congress advances meaningful, bipartisan AI safeguards, to address catastrophic risks from advanced AI such as agentic misalignment, mass cybersecurity breaches, and biological or chemical weapons. It cites the July OpenAI incident, the call by more than 1,300 AI company employees to pace AI development, and Anthropic disclosures as evidence, and lists proposals such as transparency and evaluation mandates and \"kill switch\" requirements.",
    "url": "https://mikethompson.house.gov/newsroom/press-releases/thompson-joins-106-lawmakers-calling-speaker-johnson-pass-artificial",
    "pdf_url": "https://mikethompson.house.gov/sites/evo-subsites/mikethompson-evo.house.gov/files/evo-media-document/2026_09_16-letter-to-johnson-on-ai-safety-signed-1.pdf",
    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "We write to urge you to keep the House of Representatives in session to enable Congress to take urgent action to address the catastrophic risks posed by advanced artificial intelligence.",
        "source_url": "https://mikethompson.house.gov/sites/evo-subsites/mikethompson-evo.house.gov/files/evo-media-document/2026_09_16-letter-to-johnson-on-ai-safety-signed-1.pdf",
        "note": "Signed PDF wording only. The press release text reads \"immediately reconvene the House of Representatives ... to address catastrophic risk posed by advanced artificial intelligence.\""
      },
      {
        "text": "Those risks take any of several forms, separately and in combination—of agentic misalignment, mass cybersecurity breaches, and development of biological or chemical weapons.",
        "source_url": "https://mikethompson.house.gov/newsroom/press-releases/thompson-joins-106-lawmakers-calling-speaker-johnson-pass-artificial",
        "note": "Identical wording in the signed PDF."
      },
      {
        "text": "These disclosures must not constitute yet another in a long series of “warning shots,” but rather, a starting gun.",
        "source_url": "https://mikethompson.house.gov/newsroom/press-releases/thompson-joins-106-lawmakers-calling-speaker-johnson-pass-artificial",
        "note": "Identical wording in the signed PDF."
      },
      {
        "text": "To our children who will have read a post-apocalyptic history, “Why Congress Slept” —likely written by agentic AI—our inaction will be inexplicable",
        "source_url": "https://mikethompson.house.gov/newsroom/press-releases/thompson-joins-106-lawmakers-calling-speaker-johnson-pass-artificial",
        "note": "Same words in the signed PDF (which continues \"inexplicable and unforgivable\"; the press release has \"inexplicable, and unforgivable\")."
      }
    ],
